                <pb facs="0342" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg282"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic">September 2,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister for foreign affairs sends this morning an official to say that the
                    Waller papers had left Madagascar on cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Papin</hi>,
                    which is expected toward middle of the month at Aden, from which place they will
                    be sent at once to Paris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
